DESCRIPTION:On Thursday\, Nov. 5\, from 4 to 5 p.m. at Innovate Carolina Ju
 nction in Chapel Hill\, Carolina Chief Innovation Officer Tommy Sowers hos
 ts a fireside chat with Ronit Freeman\, the UNC associate professor leadin
 g IMPEDE\, a consortium backed by up to $24.8 million from ARPA-H to detec
 t and treat protein-misfolding diseases like Alzheimer’s and pulmonary f
 ibrosis before symptoms appear. They’ll discuss how she assembled a 100-
 person\, multi-university team and an industry partner in weeks\, how AI a
 nd simulation are tackling “undruggable” proteins\, her path toward a 
 pulmonary fibrosis venture\, and how Carolina’s innovation ecosystem mov
 es discoveries toward patients. The event is aimed at faculty\, researcher
 s\, students\, entrepreneurs\, industry partners and anyone curious about 
 turning big ideas into real-world impact.
GEO:35.9143;-79.05501
LOCATION:Innovate Carolina Junction
SUMMARY:Before the First Symptom: A Fireside Chat with Ronit Freeman
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/before-the-first-symptom-a-fir
 eside-chat-with-ronit-freeman
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
