DESCRIPTION:Join UNC Global Affairs for a Diplomatic Discussion with Jim Sc
 iutto\, CNN chief national security correspondent and former chief of staf
 f to the U.S. ambassador to China. Sciutto will speak on the many fronts t
 he U.S.\, Russia\, and China\, as well as their allies\, are coming to fac
 e-to-face with one another\, such as Ukraine\, Taiwan\, the Middle East\, 
 AI and space. He will emphasize themes from his book\, The Return of Great
  Powers: Russia\, China\, and the Next World War.\n\n \n\nTuesday\, Nov. 1
 0\n5:30 p.m. (doors open at 5 p.m.)\nNelson Mandela Auditorium\, FedEx Glo
 bal Education Center\nJoin us after the discussion for pizza in the atrium
 !\n\nPlan to attend? Let us know! CLE credit is available.\n\n \n\nThe Dip
 lomatic Discussion speaker series is part of Carolina’s Diplomacy Init
 iative\, which introduces students to shared global challenges and provide
 s them opportunities to practice skills necessary to address those challen
 ges. In 2025\, UNC Global Affairs launched the Carolina Diplomacy Fellows 
 for students interested in deepening their engagement with the Diplomacy I
 nitiative. \n\n \n\nRead more about Jim Sciutto\n\nJim Sciutto is CNN’
 s chief national security analyst and anchor of “The Brief with Jim Sciu
 tto” on CNN International. Sciutto reports and provides analysis on al
 l aspects of U.S. national security including foreign policy\, the militar
 y\, intelligence community and the U.S. Department of State. Throughout hi
 s career\, he has reported from more than 50 countries across the globe\, 
 including stations in the Middle East and Ukraine. Sciutto is the author o
 f four books\, including the New York Times bestseller\, The Return of Gre
 at Powers: Russia\, China and the Next World War (2024)\, and has earned n
 umerous honors and awards. Sciutto also served as chief of staff and senio
 r advisor to the U.S. Ambassador to China\, Gary Locke. He is a graduate o
 f Yale University\, where he studied Chinese history\, and was a Fulbright
  Fellow in Hong Kong.
GEO:35.907828;-79.054177
LOCATION:FedEx Global Education Center\, Nelson Mandela Auditorium
SUMMARY:The Return of Great Powers: A Diplomatic Discussion with Jim Sciutt
 o
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/the-return-of-great-powers-a-d
 iplomatic-discussion-with-jim-sciutto
CATEGORIES:Lectures
END:VEVENT
