DESCRIPTION:This program is now FULL. To be added to our WAITLIST\, please 
 email acklandRSVP@unc.edu. \n  \nHow have artists represented the characte
 rs from Homer’s Odyssey through the centuries? How do images translate a
 nd adapt the words from this epic poem for new\, diverse audiences? \nProf
 essors Timothy Shea and Hérica Valladares\, both from UNC-Chapel Hill’s
  Department of Classics with adjunct appointments in the Department of Art
  and Art History\, will lead a seminar-style discussion focusing on works 
 from the museum’s collection\, ranging from an ancient Greek vase fragme
 nt to a twentieth-century lithograph by American artist Benton Spruance. \
 nFree\, registration required below. \n  \nThis event is part of UNC–Cha
 pel Hill’s Campus Life Experience (CLE) program. Students who attend can
  scan the QR code provided at the event to receive CLE credit.
GEO:35.912593;-79.054867
LOCATION:Ackland Art Museum
SUMMARY:An Ackland Odyssey
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/an-ackland-odyssey
CATEGORIES:Exhibits
END:VEVENT
