DESCRIPTION:The Interprofessional Design-a-thon brings together student tea
 ms to apply human-centered design thinking to address patient needs. Stude
 nt teams collaborate on a solution and present their idea to a panel of fa
 culty and health professionals\, who then select a winning team. This is a
 n approved IPEP Distinguished Scholars Immersion hosted by the Office of I
 nterprofessional Education and Practice.\n\n \n\nFall 2026 Design-a-thon:\
 n\nSaturday\, January 30 from 10 a.m. to 3 p.m.\n\nSaturday\, February 6 f
 rom 10 a.m. to 3 p.m.\n\n \n\nDesign-a-thon Eligibility:\n\nComplete basic
  BEAM Makerspace training.Be available all 5 hours on each Saturday (10 ho
 urs total) and complete independent work (research\, faculty consultation\
 , etc.) in the week between.Designed for medical\, nursing\, biomedical en
 gineering\, physical therapy\, clinical rehabilitation and mental health c
 ounseling\, occupational therapy\, speech therapy and pharmacy students. O
 ther students can apply\, and their participation will be considered as sp
 ace allows.​Applications are reviewed as received and the priority deadl
 ine to apply is December 1\, 2026. Questions? Email unc_ipe@unc.edu.
LOCATION:On Campus\, TBD
SUMMARY:Interprofessional Design-a-thon
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/interprofessional-design-a-tho
 n-2688
