DESCRIPTION:This course introduces students to Stata and data management. I
 t is tailored for non-users who want to learn how to manage data more effe
 ctively. Each day\, the class will demonstrate how to use the commands\, f
 ollowed by hands-on exercises using sample datasets. By the end of the cou
 rse\, participants will be able to perform the following:\n\n \n\n• Use 
 Stata’s Graphical User Interference (GUI) with dialog boxes\n• Run Sta
 ta commands from the command window and from scripts (“do” files)\n•
  Enter\, transfer\, and save data in different formats\, e.g.\, Excel\, SA
 S\, SPSS\, text files\n• Inspect the contents of a Stata dataset\n• Ap
 pend\, merge\, and sort datasets\n• Identify and clean duplicate records
 \n• Calculate new variables\n• Create and manage labels for variables 
 and values\n• Recode variables\n• Work with blocks of observations (
 “by” processing)\n• Perform row-wise calculations (groups of columns
 )\n• Collapse data into summary tables\n• Reshape between long and wid
 e formats\n• Save and reproduce your work with “do” files\n• Obtai
 n descriptive statistics\n• Create graphs and tables\n• Run basic stat
 istical analyses\, e.g.\, Ordinary Least Squares regression\, correlation 
 matrices\, Chi-square tests\, t-tests\n\n \n\nRegistration and fee (refund
 able for UNC-Chapel Hill students upon attendance) are required for Zoom l
 ink access.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Introduction to Stata
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/introduction-to-stata-2189
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
